WEBVTT

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:05.400
In response to the attack by mysterious giants

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.940
which happened the other day,

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.070
the government is holding a press conference.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.230
"Road Closed"

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:13.840
Our investigation has found that the giants from the other day

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:20.250
"Chief Cabinet Secretary Iwagami"

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:17.010
were weapons from Deava,

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:20.220
an anti-government terrorist organization based out of Asagaya.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.750
In addition to the giants,

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:26.960
fighter craft believed to have been launched by Deava were also sighted.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:32.730
From this, it can be inferred that Deava still possesses many dangerous weapons.

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:36.530
This leaves us in an unpredictable situation.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:35.530
"Obey"

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:39.870
Terrorists, huh? That's downright slanderous.

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:43.610
The Chief Cabinet Secretary is the minister in charge of supporting Deava.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:48.380
With him pulling a 180 like this,
Nesta must be manipulating him.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:53.650
I suppose this is what they'd call "an absolutely hopeless situation."

00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:03.490
<i>The world is engulfed by an unvoiced scream</i>

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:09.430
<i>and I wait for it to reach and stir</i> <i>a certain someone's heart</i>

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:15.240
<i>With strength flowing to the edges of our souls</i>

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:21.510
<i>we set out into the white</i> <i>morning haze, without hesitation</i>

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:24.450
<i>I want to know everything about you</i>

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:34.450
<i>But just when I thought</i>
<i>I had you, you were gone</i>

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:43.530
<i>It's love, affection, passion, expression</i>

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:50.140
<i>These tightly-sealed, silent lips</i>

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:54.510
<i>gently reply back in kind</i>

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:58.780
<i>And with love, affection, passion, expression</i>

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:05.290
<i>Now, from the last of the words I couldn't find,</i>

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:13.990
<i>the music begins</i>

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:28.740
"Listen! The Voice Calling Out to You"

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.090
No luck. It won't open.

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:37.490
What does this mean?

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:39.160
I'm not certain.

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:42.650
It's like it's being held shut by some esoteric power...

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.560
"Close"

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:46.530
A defense system that uses Verbalism?

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:47.830
Yes.

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:51.430
We're reinforcing the electric locks on the barriers with Verbalism.

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:54.840
They won't get in here for a few days using ordinary gear.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:58.940
So, it's a hybrid of modern technology and Verbalism, huh?

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:02.910
I've finished taking inventory here.
Everything matches up with the list.

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:04.850
I'm done here, too.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:08.420
Looks like our provisions will hold out for a week, at best.

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:10.450
According to an announcement by the government,

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:14.190
the many strange occurrences which took place over the past few months

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:17.460
were all caused by this Deava group.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:20.800
With many youths included in their membership,

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:26.200
we will have to wait for further news to discover their motives.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:27.700
Hey, this is...

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:28.970
"I found the list."

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:28.970
"What's this?"

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:28.970
"The Deava members list! It's classified info."

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:31.710
"Akira Kaibuki"

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:31.710
"Maia Tsukigane"

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:31.710
"Kokone Kikogami"

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:31.710
There's a list out already?

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:35.540
This is making us look like real criminals!

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:38.750
Here.

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:41.080
This one is yours, Shoko.

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:42.650
I don't want it.

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:44.810
I understand how you must feel, but...

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:56.230
If you don't eat properly, you'll collapse.

00:03:56.230 --> 00:04:00.940
W-We didn't just lose M-Maia, we lost Ts-Tsutomu, too...

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:03.100
B-But...

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:11.250
Akira, i-isn't there anything I can do to h-help?

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:14.180
I w-want to give you strength!

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:17.190
I'm not worth your time.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.810
That's not...!

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:30.270
I... can't become... the savior.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:34.300
In the end, all I did was make him suffer.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:35.790
Him...

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:41.680
"Him"? Who is that?

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:49.280
I don't know! I can't remember!

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:55.720
Well, if I don't know,
I guess it doesn't matter.

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:58.130
You're even going to let go of your awareness of him?

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:02.870
Well, that does seem fitting for a puppet to do.

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:04.730
You again?

00:05:04.730 --> 00:05:08.300
Nesta, was it? What do you even want to do?

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:12.470
Oh, my objective is very simple to understand.

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:17.240
I want to end this civilization.
Using Aquarion Logos.

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:21.020
This is Aquarion Logos...

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:26.090
Yeah, your machines aren't at a sufficient level for it yet.

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:31.560
This adds two remote-controlled
Vectors to the Gattai to compensate.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:33.030
When will it be ready?

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:37.670
Don't rush me. You must need some time to rest and recover, too.

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:39.540
What are you getting at?

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:43.670
Did you think I hadn't noticed your health issues?

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:47.740
The Truth Tribe, who were pushed to the brink by the Writing Tribe,

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:51.580
needed something to turn around their fortunes in battle.

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:56.190
And what they got their hands on was Kiryu's dead body.

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:59.960
Using it, they created the Book of Verbalism.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.120
As the heir to Kiryu's power,

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:05.930
it makes sense that you can use yourself as a Book of Verbalism.

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:10.800
However, there's no way a human body could survive that sort of stress.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:13.370
I can't put anything past you, Mr. Hayashi.

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:16.740
Is stopping here not an option?

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:21.110
It isn't. I have to defeat Akira Kaibuki.

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:24.380
That will decide whether or not
I can remain myself.

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:26.380
Why are you so fixated on that?

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:29.220
I spent my whole life looking at my father.

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:33.560
Hoping that he'd notice me, I chased after a man I could never reach.

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:39.330
But, the moment when I thought
I could see his face, Dad died.

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:42.770
Akira Kaibuki was the one who happened to be there at the time.

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:47.940
Ultimately, I'm not a person who can live on my own.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:53.400
I need something to cling to.
And now, he's all I've got.

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:57.810
How long are you going to sulk?

00:06:57.810 --> 00:06:59.750
To get out of this situation,

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:04.850
we need to return the politicians being controlled by the book back to normal.

00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:06.960
Only Vector-Ga can do that.

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:10.760
Akira, we need your power.

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:12.630
Akira!

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:16.470
I can't do it. Not anymore.

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:21.600
Don't give me that! If we give up here, what did Tsutomu die for?!

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:25.670
I can't do it. Only you can.

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:29.010
Please, Akira. You're the savior, aren't you?

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:31.850
I'm not a savior anymore.

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:33.650
Huh?

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:38.620
What happened with Tsutomu and Vector-Ga is our fault, not...

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:43.120
Leave me alone. I can't save anyone anymore.

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:56.370
I... I... I...!

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:04.050
This is our fault for relying on you too heavily.

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:05.540
I'm sorry.

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:08.370
Akira.

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:17.560
I... I'm terrible.

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:21.700
I p-pushed my ideals onto him...

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:22.670
"Akira"

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:31.240
Who was I just talking about?

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:33.510
This may have been for the best.

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:38.170
If what Maia was saying is right, he shouldn't pilot Vector-Ga anymore.

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:39.180
"Akira"

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:41.220
What do you mean?

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:44.790
The pilot of Vector-Ga... Huh?

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.280
"Akira"

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:51.020
Who were we talking about again?

00:08:54.030 --> 00:08:57.090
It's meaningless for me to be here now.

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:01.040
The disappearance of a concept.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:04.610
When the concept of Akira has fully vanished,

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:08.880
no one will be able to register your existence.

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:12.550
However, for me, who has the Book of Verbalism,

00:09:12.550 --> 00:09:15.880
the concept of that word will likely never vanish.

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:17.420
Akira,

00:09:17.420 --> 00:09:21.590
even if no one else in the world can notice your existence,

00:09:21.590 --> 00:09:24.390
you will never disappear from inside of me.

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:28.500
That is why I will win.

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:32.100
I will push you to the brink, and then over it!

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:36.400
Rejoice. I shall now set you free.

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:46.140
"Electricity"

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:55.590
A power outage?

00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:56.960
That can't be right!

00:09:56.960 --> 00:10:00.460
This base has its own generator!

00:10:00.460 --> 00:10:02.660
Could this possibly be...?

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:16.450
Electricity is the lifeline of modern civilization.

00:10:16.450 --> 00:10:21.850
To take it from them with an electricity M.J.B.K.? You're merciless.

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:24.650
Were you with Maia again?

00:10:24.650 --> 00:10:27.790
She's so pitiful, I can't bear to watch.

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:33.700
Memories from her failed attempt at playing human must be hurting that doll.

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:39.800
Why not just let her forget it all?

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:42.830
You must know how to do it.

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:55.380
That took a while.
Don't let your guard down!

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:04.160
Looks like batteries won't work, either.

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:06.760
Electricity has stopped flowing entirely.

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:09.770
Sakurako, it seems they've broken through Shirobaco's back door.

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:11.000
What?!

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:14.170
We've let the enemy get inside, then?

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:17.010
And we need to be dealing with the M.J.B.K. now, too...

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:19.270
Th-The Vectors will move, right?

00:11:19.270 --> 00:11:22.740
We should be able to activate the
Vectors themselves with just Verbalism.

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:26.180
But, if the base systems are down, we can't launch.

00:11:26.180 --> 00:11:30.350
We could shoot through all the walls with our Vectors and break out!

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:33.590
That's impossible. Though we can activate them with Verbalism,

00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:37.680
the firing system relies on electricity.
We probably can't use it now.

00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:43.230
We're going in! They're just past here! Move!

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:48.370
If you use the ducts in the rear of the elevator shaft,

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:51.540
it should be possible to escape without running into the enemy.

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:55.380
Kujyo, Kikogami, Uminagi, you three go.

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:57.050
Commander, that's...!

00:11:57.050 --> 00:12:01.150
The worst imaginable outcome here would be to lose you kids.

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:04.550
If that happened, there would be nobody left to fight the M.J.B.K.

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:06.590
B-But, the Vectors...!

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:08.460
Of course, I have no intention of letting them take those.

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:11.890
We'll stay here and hold out until the last.

00:12:11.890 --> 00:12:16.730
But, even if we lose them, there's sure to be a chance to take them back.

00:12:16.730 --> 00:12:18.430
As long as you three are safe.

00:12:18.430 --> 00:12:20.900
Don't we get any say in this?!

00:12:20.900 --> 00:12:23.770
Sorry for being such an unfair adult.

00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:32.280
--Come along.
--H-Hey! Big Brother!

00:12:32.280 --> 00:12:36.180
--Kikogami, you too!
--Shoko, you should evacuate, too.

00:12:36.180 --> 00:12:37.740
I●●●

00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:58.110
Hey, you kids, what are you doing?

00:12:58.110 --> 00:13:00.010
Oh, crap!

00:13:00.010 --> 00:13:01.500
Hey!

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:10.220
Someone, help!

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:11.550
What happened?

00:13:11.550 --> 00:13:12.950
Are you okay?

00:13:12.950 --> 00:13:14.660
This is awful!

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:16.730
Let's go to the first-aid station north of here.

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:18.830
Help me!

00:13:18.830 --> 00:13:20.630
Somebody!

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:23.860
"Akira"

00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:31.370
I lost the others...

00:13:33.210 --> 00:13:35.180
You're one of the bad guys!

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:37.250
I... I read it online!

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:38.750
N-No!

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:40.650
Don't run away!

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:45.880
Look out!

00:13:53.090 --> 00:13:56.330
No good. I can't get through to Kikogami.

00:13:56.330 --> 00:14:01.930
The Aquariphone ought to work even without electricity, though...

00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:06.170
Karan?

00:14:06.170 --> 00:14:08.440
Hey, Big Brother Hayato...

00:14:08.440 --> 00:14:12.410
We were fighting to protect everyone, right?

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:15.420
So why does this have to happen to us?!

00:14:15.420 --> 00:14:19.290
Don't you normally get praised for doing good things?

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:21.360
Yes, that's right, Karan.

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:24.260
Good deeds should be met with proper recognition.

00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:26.960
This is not how things should be!

00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:28.800
Found them!

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:30.370
This way! This way!

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:32.030
Circle around that way!

00:14:37.470 --> 00:14:39.070
Are you okay?

00:14:43.910 --> 00:14:47.420
S-Someone! Is anyone there?!

00:14:47.420 --> 00:14:51.440
Please, notice us! Someone!

00:14:53.050 --> 00:14:56.490
Someone! Please, someone!

00:14:57.660 --> 00:15:02.060
It's no good... I can't reach... anyone...

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:08.130
You're like a stray dog.

00:15:10.310 --> 00:15:12.570
Grandpa...

00:15:12.240 --> 00:15:16.970
"Kaibuki"

00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:14.910
We were really worried.

00:15:14.910 --> 00:15:16.750
I'm sorry.

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:24.480
Try writing it.

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:43.370
They're terrorists, I hear. How scary.

00:15:43.370 --> 00:15:46.110
How many people do you think have died because of you?

00:15:46.110 --> 00:15:48.940
Say something, you murderers!

00:15:48.940 --> 00:15:49.950
Shut up!

00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:52.610
--Hey.
--I get that you feel uneasy,

00:15:52.610 --> 00:15:57.850
but finding an easy outlet for your anger won't solve the problem!

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:00.190
Have you really thought about this for yourself?

00:16:00.190 --> 00:16:03.990
Is this incident something a human could actually cause?

00:16:03.990 --> 00:16:06.360
Did you stop and decide for yourself?

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:11.570
To call this young girl a murderer?

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:13.570
What's this guy's problem?

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:16.140
I'll shout it out as many times as I have to!

00:16:16.140 --> 00:16:18.230
We were not wrong!

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:21.580
H-Hayato?

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:24.250
Are you there, Hayato?

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:28.480
He's not... But his voice reached me!

00:16:28.480 --> 00:16:31.320
Could it be... V-Verbalism?!

00:16:33.820 --> 00:16:36.160
In the right place at the right time.

00:16:36.160 --> 00:16:40.030
Words given voice at the proper time take on power.

00:16:41.330 --> 00:16:45.270
Right now, what I want to say from the bottom of my heart is...

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:47.830
"Sing"

00:16:54.680 --> 00:17:02.280
♪ Why? Why is it? ♪

00:17:02.280 --> 00:17:09.860
♪ Since the time I was a child, ♪

00:17:07.760 --> 00:17:09.920
Akira.

00:17:09.860 --> 00:17:18.030
♪ I have thought, God, ♪

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:12.060
Has it been seven years now?

00:17:12.060 --> 00:17:16.630
Since we took you in because you had nowhere to go.

00:17:16.630 --> 00:17:19.530
When we first met, you said something.

00:17:18.030 --> 00:17:24.710
♪ why is everything so unfair? ♪

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:22.770
That you had to become the savior.

00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:28.310
Those words must have been the very essence of your soul.

00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:31.950
♪ Like the mermaid who was forced to choose ♪

00:17:28.310 --> 00:17:29.810
I●●●

00:17:31.950 --> 00:17:39.050
♪ between her voice and her love, ♪

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:34.750
It will reach him! I'm sure of it!

00:17:37.990 --> 00:17:40.290
Akira?

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:46.560
♪ and then ultimately

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:46.560
was able to have neither, ♪

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:42.390
I can hear it.

00:17:42.390 --> 00:17:43.890
She's calling me.

00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:53.300
♪ and was turned to sea foam ♪

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:55.240
Huh?

00:17:55.240 --> 00:17:57.570
Please, release them at once.

00:17:57.570 --> 00:18:00.310
S-Senator Kobayakawa?! Why?!

00:18:00.310 --> 00:18:04.810
I've come here on official government orders. They are innocent.

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:06.410
But...

00:18:09.950 --> 00:18:12.510
Senator Kobayakawa, what is going on?

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:19.760
The truth isn't the only way to move people.

00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:22.930
Lies are what you make of them, Hayato Kujyo.

00:18:27.270 --> 00:18:30.170
Mom! Tinoa!

00:18:34.640 --> 00:18:36.880
Don't move!

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:40.280
If you do anything more, I'll trigger this craft's self-destruct mechanism!

00:18:40.280 --> 00:18:41.720
Shoko?!

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:43.280
Shoko?

00:18:43.280 --> 00:18:47.810
There's nothing left I can do.
Maybe I should just end it all...

00:18:54.300 --> 00:18:57.490
"A lovey-dovey date with Shoko!"

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:01.640
This is...

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:04.910
I wonder if Shoko smiled for me.

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:08.340
--Huh?!
--Don't you make a guy's girlfriend cry!

00:19:08.340 --> 00:19:12.680
I really do like Shoko best when she's smiling.

00:19:12.680 --> 00:19:14.170
His voice...

00:19:17.020 --> 00:19:20.050
No! I have to smile!

00:19:18.490 --> 00:19:23.220
"Smile"

00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:23.160
Tsutomu brought smiles back to the world.

00:19:23.160 --> 00:19:26.560
I have to live on and keep smiling!

00:19:34.440 --> 00:19:41.410
♪ The voice I heard ♪

00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:48.850
♪ has resounded through my whole body ♪

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:56.690
♪ I will let this voice you believed in resound, ♪

00:19:56.690 --> 00:20:03.290
♪ and I will walk forward ♪

00:20:05.030 --> 00:20:12.710
♪ For tomorrow's voice,

00:20:05.030 --> 00:20:12.710
when yesterday ends, ♪

00:20:12.710 --> 00:20:15.910
♪ you can try listening... ♪

00:20:16.810 --> 00:20:18.580
Akira!

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:37.800
Akira?

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:39.930
I heard your voice.

00:20:39.930 --> 00:20:45.840
If there are voices seeking salvation,
I will always be there to extend a hand.

00:20:45.840 --> 00:20:47.400
For I am...

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:04.190
Listen, when Maia vanished,
I thought it might be my chance.

00:21:04.190 --> 00:21:09.650
B-But, I really hated myself for thinking that way.

00:21:11.430 --> 00:21:13.430
What I love about you

00:21:13.430 --> 00:21:20.140
is the way you're so straightforward in doing what you need to do.

00:21:20.140 --> 00:21:25.010
So, tell me, what do you need to do right now?

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:28.180
Who do you truly want to save?

00:21:29.620 --> 00:21:31.850
I●●●

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:34.120
I want to save Maia!

00:21:35.390 --> 00:21:37.020
I know.

00:21:39.530 --> 00:21:41.020
I have to go.

00:21:46.070 --> 00:21:47.900
Wait, she is...

00:21:47.900 --> 00:21:51.210
Mr. Sakamoto, what are you doing here?

00:21:51.210 --> 00:21:55.470
Shoko, I didn't realize you were still working here.

00:21:58.180 --> 00:22:02.720
No. This must be a message for me.

00:22:02.720 --> 00:22:04.720
I have a request.

00:22:04.720 --> 00:22:09.390
Please bring me to my father,
Secretary Iwagami.

00:22:09.390 --> 00:22:11.990
--Huh?!
--Shoko?

00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:25.770
<i>I want to lend you a true voice</i>

00:22:35.850 --> 00:22:41.190
<i>With the warmth of salvation,</i>
<i>I raise my hand into the sky</i>

00:22:41.190 --> 00:22:45.930
<i>and everything in the world gains its true colors</i>

00:22:45.930 --> 00:22:48.600
<i>(Focus) A sound that was once hidden</i>

00:22:48.600 --> 00:22:51.700
<i>(on the goal) will connect us now</i>

00:22:51.700 --> 00:22:54.200
<i>Try to understand that, okay?</i>

00:22:54.200 --> 00:22:56.640
<i>So, are you ready?</i>

00:22:56.640 --> 00:22:59.440
<i>(heart and soul) These silent teardrops</i>

00:22:59.440 --> 00:23:02.040
<i>(narrow escape) that flow forth now</i>

00:23:02.040 --> 00:23:05.550
<i>(enamored) are proof of that person's existence</i>

00:23:05.550 --> 00:23:12.050
<i>You can't go inside your heart all alone</i>

00:23:12.050 --> 00:23:14.620
<i>I will hesitate no more</i>

00:23:14.620 --> 00:23:19.790
<i>I want to lend you a true voice</i>

00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:25.000
<i>A useful life, a sparkling utopia</i>

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:34.110
<i>When your heart and voice</i> <i>tremble together, you'll surpass all</i>

00:23:34.110 --> 00:23:37.510
<i>So go for your heart</i>

00:23:50.290 --> 00:23:52.630
Hey, Maia, what were you like in elementary school?

00:23:52.630 --> 00:23:54.160
I trained every day.

00:23:54.160 --> 00:23:55.800
Okay, while I'm asking, how about you, Subete?

00:23:55.800 --> 00:23:57.770
I played with Maia in our secret base every day.

00:23:57.770 --> 00:23:59.600
You were pushy, so I reluctantly played along.

00:23:59.600 --> 00:24:00.130
That's mean!

00:24:00.130 --> 00:24:02.670
You ate my dirt dumplings and drank my mud cider like they were delicious.

00:24:02.670 --> 00:24:04.270
You two were close, huh?

00:24:04.270 --> 00:24:06.470
Yes. Next time, on Episode 23:

00:24:05.170 --> 00:24:08.140
"Episode 23: Revive! The Vow

00:24:05.170 --> 00:24:08.140
Beneath the Moonlight"

00:24:06.470 --> 00:24:08.310
"Revive! The Vow Beneath the Moonlight."

00:24:08.310 --> 00:24:09.710
I asked something I shouldn't have...
